Reproduced on Flutter 3.47.4 stable (9584c6713b), Chrome on macOS. The code involved is unchanged on master 697012a97f (links below).

### Steps to reproduce

1. Run `flutter build web` on the code sample below, serve the build and open it in Chrome.
2. Turn semantics on: run `document.querySelector('flt-semantics-placeholder').click()` in the console, or use a screen reader.
3. Inspect the checkbox's `flt-semantics` element, or the checkbox in Chrome's accessibility tree.

### Expected results

The checkbox has `aria-checked="mixed"`, so a screen reader announces it as "mixed" or "partially checked".

### Actual results

The checkbox has `aria-checked="false"`, so a screen reader announces it as not checked.

The framework side is correct: the semantics node for the same checkbox has `isChecked == CheckedState.mixed` (see the widget test under Logs). The value is lost in the web engine.

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(
  MaterialApp(
    home: Scaffold(
      body: Checkbox(tristate: true, value: null, onChanged: (_) {}, semanticLabel: 'Team'),
    ),
  ),
);
```

</details>

### Screenshots or Video

Not applicable: the logs below are the evidence.

### Logs

<details open><summary>Logs</summary>

The checkbox's DOM element and its node in Chrome's accessibility tree:

```
DOM <flt-semantics id="flt-semantic-node-4" tabindex="0" aria-label="Team" flt-tappable="" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" …>
AX  checkbox "Team" checked="false"
```

The widget test below, run on the same code sample, prints:

```
checkbox: isChecked=CheckedState.mixed
```

</details>

<details><summary>Widget test showing the framework sends CheckedState.mixed</summary>

