While reviewing https://github.com/flutter/packages/pull/13029, Gemini pointed out an existing issue here: https://github.com/flutter/packages/pull/13029#discussion_r4112023872

In `CupertinoMagnifier`, `focalPointOffset.scale()` returns a new `Offset` instead of modifying the existing one. As a result, the animation scale is currently ignored.

The problematic code is:

```dart
var focalPointOffset = Offset(
  0,
  (size.height / 2) - kMagnifierAboveFocalPoint,
);
focalPointOffset.scale(1, inOutAnimation?.value ?? 1); // No effect
focalPointOffset += additionalFocalPointOffset;
```

## Expected Behavior
The `focalPointOffset` should be scaled correctly by the animation value.

## Proposed Fix
The return value of `.scale()` should be assigned back to the variable, or chained directly during the initialization of `focalPointOffset`:

```dart
var focalPointOffset = Offset(0, (size.height / 2) - kMagnifierAboveFocalPoint)
    .scale(1, inOutAnimation?.value ?? 1);
focalPointOffset += additionalFocalPointOffset;
```

A corresponding widget test should also be added to assert that `rawMagnifier.focalPointOffset` correctly scales when `inOutAnimation` is set.

