### Expected results

`HasPipeline` and `GetPipeline` can run on one thread while another thread creates pipelines, as Flutter GPU does.

### Actual results

`PipelineLibraryGLES` locks `programs_` but not `pipelines_`, and `GetPipeline` inserts into `pipelines_` on the calling thread (only program linking runs on the reactor). Flutter GPU calls `HasPipeline` and `GetPipeline` on the UI thread (`RenderPass::GetOrCreatePipeline`) while Impeller inserts variants on the raster thread.

- The test fails in 32 of 40 runs: the reader thread misses a pipeline that already exists.
- Under TSan, all 10 runs report the race between `GetPipeline` (insert) and `HasPipeline` (lookup).
- With a mutex on `pipelines_`, it passes 40/40 and TSan reports no `pipelines_` race.

This is confirmed only with this engine test on Linux (Mesa), not in an app. It is a sibling of #193721 (Metal pipelines) and #193737 (samplers).

