`GetSampler` scans the plain `samplers_` vector and then calls `push_back`, with no lock. Flutter GPU calls it on the UI thread (`RenderPass.bindTexture`), and Impeller calls it on the raster thread (for example `FramebufferBlendContents::Render`). A scan can read a buffer that `push_back` is reallocating. Two inserts at once can corrupt the vector or drop a sampler that was already returned.

- Metal (macOS): TSan reports the race in the code sample in 4 of 6 runs on master.
