A bundled native asset is recorded by bare file name on a desktop build, and the engine hands that to `dlopen`, so it resolves through the dynamic linker instead of from the bundle. The manifest has a `relative` kind that should cover this, but on embedder-API platforms it resolves against a debug label, so it cannot be used either. A packaged app therefore has no way to load its own bundled native assets without putting their directory on the global linker search path.

Verified at 3.47.5.

## The tool writes a bare name

`flutter_tools/lib/src/isolated/native_assets/native_assets.dart`, `_targetLocationSingleArchitecture`:

```dart
case DynamicLoadingBundled _:
  final String fileName = asset.codeAsset.file!.pathSegments.last;
  if (absolutePath != null) {
    // Flutter tester needs full host paths.
    uri = absolutePath.resolve(fileName);
  } else {
    // Flutter Desktop needs "absolute" paths inside the app.
    uri = Uri(path: fileName);
  }
```

`absolutePath` is non-null only for the tester: `final Uri? absolutePath = flutterTester ? buildUri : null;`. So a real build emits a name with no directory:

```json
{"format-version":[1,0,0],"native-assets":{"linux_riscv64":{
  "package:sqlite3/src/ffi/libsqlite3.g.dart":["system","libsqlite3.so"],
  "package:appstream_dart/src/appstream_native.dart":["absolute","libappstream.so"]}}}
```

## The engine dlopens it as-is

`runtime/dart_isolate.cc` `NativeAssetsDlopen` sends `kAbsolute` to `dart::bin::NativeAssets::DlopenAbsolute`, which is `dlopen` of that string. With no slash the dynamic linker resolves it: `DT_RUNPATH`, `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, `ld.so.cache`, default directories. The asset store is not consulted -- `NativeAssetsManager` parses the manifest and nothing else (`assets/native_assets.cc`).

Bundling the library is therefore not enough. Its directory has to go on the global search path, which puts every app's libraries in one namespace: two apps bundling different versions of a library get whichever `ld.so.cache` lists first.

## `relative` cannot be used

flutter_tools documents the kind as what we want:

```dart
// "relative" in the context of native assets would be relative to the
// kernel or aot snapshot.
```

The engine resolves it against `advisory_script_uri`:

```cpp
static void* NativeAssetsDlopenRelative(const char* path, char** error) {
  const std::string& script_uri = (*isolate_group_data)->GetAdvisoryScriptURI();
  return dart::bin::NativeAssets::DlopenRelative(path, script_uri.data(), error);
}
```

That is a debug label, not a path. `common/settings.h` defaults it to `"main.dart"`, and nothing exposes it to an embedder:

- `shell/platform/embedder/embedder.cc` never sets it, and no `FlutterProjectArgs` field maps to it
- `shell/common/switches.{h,cc}` has no switch, so `command_line_argv` cannot carry it
- only the in-tree iOS and Fuchsia embedders set it, from `libraryURI` and `debug_label_`

