## Summary

`Paint.isAntiAlias = false` is lost when no earlier draw in the same `Picture` set anti-aliasing to `true`. `DisplayListBuilder` starts from `DlPaint`, whose anti-alias default is `false`, and records `SetAntiAlias` only when the value changes. Impeller's dispatcher starts every display list, including nested ones, from `impeller::Paint()`, whose `anti_alias` default is `true`. So when the first anti-alias-relevant draw of a picture asks for `false`, nothing is recorded, and Impeller draws it with anti-aliasing.

Since #186020 (fixing #185834), `isAntiAlias = false` is the way to keep a draw off the UberSDF path. For a paint with a color source that path is the three-pass fallback described in #192994. Because of this mismatch the opt-out does not work in the common case: one shader rect in its own `CustomPaint`, or the first draw after `drawPicture`.

On an M3 Max, one shader rect costs about 125 µs with the flag lost and 7.5 µs with it honoured. The two paths also produce different pixels.

